In article <1992Jan31.074504.10252@vax5.cit.cornell.edu> yqdx@vax5.cit.cornell.edu writes:

     By the way, I was thinking that one way of accumulating scrolls could be
   to send MAIL to yourself, and polymorph the scrolls of mail.  (I always
   seem to run out of scrolls first on my big polypiling binges.)  Is there
   any way to do this with Amiga nethack?  Thanks for your help.


Don't know about Amiga, but it doesn't work on unix.  I tried it.  They don't 
polymorph.  Probably all for the best, though:  if scrolls could be polymorphed
FROM mail, they also should be able to be polymorphed INTO mail.  It would all
be pretty amusing (What _does_ the mail daemon write in his spare time?) but it
would mean a waste of potentially useful scrolls you were hoping would turn
into something else.

As I remember, you can't even make blank scrolls out of them by dipping them.  
Guess the dev team's a step ahead of us ;^)

